  "articleBody": "After a fire, you might be wondering if you can handle the cleanup yourself. While you might be tempted to tackle small smoke spots, most fire damage situations really do call for professional intervention. If you see visible charring, extensive soot deposits, or any structural concerns, it's definitely time to call in the pros. Also, if there's significant water damage from firefighting efforts, that complicates things quickly. Even a lingering smoke odor indicates widespread damage that DIY methods usually can't resolve. Professional restoration companies like First To Respond Restoration have the specialized equipment, training, and expertise to safely and effectively mitigate fire and smoke damage, removing odors, cleaning surfaces, and restoring your property properly. We serve the San Fernando Valley and surrounding areas, offering 24-hour emergency services to address these complex situations.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-21"
